.TH CW "1" "October 2026" "cw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cw \- cw close
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cw
\fI\,close \/\fR[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] [\fI\,NAME\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
Save state and close windows of a Context.
.IP
Without NAME, closes the current window (asks for confirmation). NAME can be
"ContextName" (close all) or "ContextName/WindowName" (one window). State is
saved before closing ??? if save fails, close is aborted.
.IP
Examples:
.TP
cw close
close current window (confirm)
.TP
cw close \fB\-y\fR
close current window (no confirm)
.TP
cw close MyProject
close all windows in Context
.TP
cw close MyProject/Development
close one window
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation when closing current window.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this message and exit.
